course: dictionary
lesson: 7856
title: Rafters: the beams that hold up a roof
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rafter is one of the long, sloping pieces of wood that hold up a roof. Picture a house roof: the rafters run from the top of the roof down to the walls. «Ham, herbs, onions and eggs hang from the rafters» tells you they are fixed high up, to the beams of the roof.
explain: Rafters is also used in a phrase. «The hall was packed to the rafters.» A hall cannot be packed into wooden beams, so the words hall and packed are the clue. Packed to the rafters means completely full of people or things.
explain: Always check your meaning in the sentence. Swap "completely full" in for "packed to the rafters": "The hall was completely full" still makes sense, so you are right. Some words only mean something special inside a set phrase, so read the words around them.
fact: A rafter is one of the long, sloping beams of wood that holds up a roof.
fact: Owls, bats and swallows often nest in the rafters of barns.
fact: «Packed to the rafters» means completely full of people or things.
fact: «The cheers shook the rafters» means the cheering was very loud.
fact: Rafters is the plural of rafter, so it means more than one beam.
exercise: «Ham, herbs, onions and eggs hang from the rafters.» Where are the hams hanging? | On the floor | In a bowl on the table | In the garden | *From the beams of the roof
exercise: «The hall was packed to the rafters.» What does packed to the rafters mean? | Packed into a box | Very quiet and empty | *Completely full | Very tall and narrow
exercise: «The cheers shook the rafters.» What does this sentence tell you about the cheers? | Very quiet | Sad and slow | *Very loud | Cold and wet
test: «Owls and swallows nested in the rafters of the old barn.» What are rafters? | *Long sloping beams that hold up a roof | Small windows in a wall | Ropes for swings
test: Dad says, «The bus was packed to the rafters.» What does he mean? | The bus had no roof | *The bus was completely full | The bus was very old | The bus was driving very fast
exam: Which word means a long sloping beam that holds up a roof? | Chimney | Settle | *Rafter | Trestle
